{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/353058-question-about-limit-of-contracts-by-wyrd","id":353058,"title":"Question about limit of contracts by Wyrd.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-28T13:34:43-08:00","id":353058,"title":"Question about limit of contracts by Wyrd.","content":"Hello, im preparing to run a Changeling game and reading through the Core rulebook on page 84 i saw the wyrd table that say that &quot;Attribute/Skill/Contract Maximum&quot; for wyrd less than 5 is 5 for all of those things. Attribute and skills are pretty straight foward but contracts isnt so clear for me and my table.<br /> <br /> Does it mean that a character can only have 5 different categories of contracts? For example. Lets says fairest with wyrd 5 having Vainglory (1 to 5), Separation (1 to 5), Fleeting summer (1 to 5), Eternal Summer (1 to 5) and Punishing summer (1 to 5)<br /> <br /> Or does it mean that a character with wyrd 5 can only have 5 contract regardless of category. For example he could start with Separation Contract from 1 to 5 and that would be his limit.<br /> <br /> Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-28T14:00:46-08:00","id":353106,"title":"","content":"It's likely an artifact of earlier designs that slipped through. Some White Wolf games have traditionally had exceptionally powerful dot levels for magic powers that require a higher power stat to purchase. Changeling: the Lost did not end up having any contracts with 6+ dot clauses, but that's typically what that language means, in the absence of a specification otherwise: a Wyrd 6+ changeling could theoretically develop advanced contract clauses that exceed the fifth dot clause.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-28T14:21:41-08:00","id":353133,"title":"","content":"SL is correct. It just means one could, hypothetically, get level 6+ contracts with 6+ Wyrd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum